---
description: Mobile layout and overflow rules for UI and CSS
globs:
  - src/components/**/*.tsx
  - src/app/**/*.tsx
  - src/app/**/*.css
alwaysApply: false
---

Give every flex and grid child `min-width: 0` (`min-w-0`). Do not set a fixed width larger than its parent.

A wide piece (contribution calendar, CodeMirror, diagram SVG) needs a wrapper with `width: 100%`, `max-width: 100%`, `min-width: 0`, `overflow-x: auto`, and `contain: paint`. On mobile Chrome, a wide table or grid widens the layout viewport even inside `overflow: auto`. `contain: inline-size` does not stop that. `innerWidth` grows with it, so check `scrollWidth` against `clientWidth`.

`overflow-x: clip` on `html`, `body`, and `main` is fine. Do not set overflow on `.shell`; that breaks the sticky rail.

Tap targets are at least 44px. Check light and dark. Do not put `--vision-*` in `@theme` or `@property`.
